            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The disclosure concerns a method of a user equipment for wireless communication, the method comprising: receiving, from a base station, configuration information for a channel state information reference signal, CSI-RS, resource set comprising CSI-RS resources, the CSI-RS resources being grouped into a first group and a second group; identifying CSI associated with at least two CSI-RS resources from the CSI-RS resource set; determining a CSI report to include a CSI reference signal resource indicator, CRI, corresponding to the at least two CSI-RS resource associated with the identified CSI; and transmitting, to the base station, the determined CSI report, wherein the CSI associated with the at least two CSI-RS resources is associated with a first CSI-RS resource from the first group and a second CSI-RS resource from the second group, and the CRI is associated with a resource pair consisted of the first resource from the first group and the second CSI-RS resource from the second group.</p>
            </abstract>
